From 60ea68dd6d10b82b5f727102fce991a3762a0cbb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:04:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add shen_erl_compiler_api, a public compiler and dispatch
 interface

Embedders (other backends, code generators, Erlang callers) had to use
internal functions: shen_erl_kl_codegen:compile/1 registers a defun in
the function store before compiling it, eval/1 always loads, and
dispatch lives in shen_erl_kl_compiler:invoke/2.

shen_erl_compiler_api splits compilation into steps with a documented,
-spec'd contract:

  parse_string/1, parse_file/1  KLambda source -> KL forms
  forms/2                       KL forms -> Erlang abstract forms
  compile/2                     KL forms -> BEAM binary
  load/2                        load the binary, register its defuns
  run_toplevel/1                run the module's non-defun forms
  call/2, arity/1, lookup/1     runtime dispatch by name

forms/2 and compile/2 load nothing and change no function binding.  To
make that possible the code generator no longer needs a defun to be
registered before it is compiled: the defuns of the forms being
compiled are passed down in the compile environment and shadow the
function store, with the same overridability rule as set_mfa.  eval/1
now compiles that way and registers in the new codegen load/2, after
loading the module; the generated code is the same as before.
compile/1, compile/3 (used by the kernel build after load_defuns/2) and
the stores are otherwise unchanged.

Adds shen_erl_global_stores:is_overridable/1 and the
shen_erl_compiler_api_SUITE Common Test suite.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01V3S3SEmxSj7HnbJJmxMhCJ
